  "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $(\u00acA\u2227B)\u2228(\u00acA\u2227C)?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we can factor out the conjunction with $\u00acA,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(\u00acA\u2227B)\u2228(\u00acA\u2227C)\u2261\u00acA\u2227(B\u2228C)\n$$\n\nThen, since $B\u2228C\u2261C\u2228B,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\u00acA\u2227(B\u2228C)\u2261\u00acA\u2227(C\u2228B).\n$$",
